# Snapshots are tenant data — customer names, addresses, order values. They are
# NOT committed by default: this repo has a UK tenant, and a full table snapshot
# sitting in git history is a subject-access problem nobody wants to discover
# later.
#
# To keep one deliberately as the record of an operation (the way
# mcr_backup_residue_2026-09-16.json is kept), add it by force and say in the
# commit message what it holds and why it is small enough to keep:
#
#   git add -f scripts/snapshots/<file>.json
*.json
!.gitignore
